From 1bfa2c49ab67cc60b215864602ad848863a6a30e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 08:26:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dsv41): align moe_swiglu_cast with DeepSeek
 Expert.forward BF16 rounding

Base: 2756478b60b9 (1107 patch 0761)
Rationale: In DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash reference (inference/model.py:843-853),
  Expert.forward computes x = F.silu(gate) * up; x = weights * x; and passes
  x.to(torch.bfloat16) to self.w2, which quantizes the BF16 activation to MXFP8
  via act_quant. The shared expert kernel (activation.py:swiglu_clamp_cast_kernel)
  already rounds the FP32 SwiGLU product to BF16 before computing amax and
  get_sf_and_inv, whereas routed moe_swiglu_cast previously quantized the
  unrounded FP32 __expf/__fdividef product directly and carried a warp-vote
  certificate fallback pass. Rounding (val_l / (1 + exp(-val_l))) * val_r * weight
  to bfloat16 before amax and get_sf_and_inv makes routed moe_swiglu_cast
  100% byte-for-byte identical to DeepSeek Expert.forward across all TP4 (576)
  and TP3 (768) shapes and decode/mid/prefill tile heights (0 FP8 byte diffs,
  0 UE8M0 scale diffs), eliminates the 87.9% per-layer BF16 ULP divergence in
  end-to-end MoE outputs (0 ULP diffs vs _arithmetic reference even after 10
  stacked MoE residual layers), and removes the warp-vote certificate pass
  (1.01x-1.25x faster decode/mid SwiGLU kernel latency).
Quality: Bit-identical to DeepSeek reference Expert.forward + act_quant (0 FP8
  byte diffs and 0 scale diffs across 37.9M tested elements; 0 ULP diffs vs
  _arithmetic reference in test_moe_reference_separates_defects at rows=12 and
  rows=300).
Tests: pytest tests/kernels/moe/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_moe.py
  tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_activation.py (165 passed, 0 PDL
  violations).
Upstream status: spark-ds41f local patch (#1018).
